From a364e92ac31fcdd4fab181c055f33e9689e68af7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:42:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 02/17] feat(mcp): send each tool's _agentNote once per session

Every insight-create returned the same 649-token _agentNote, every
insight-update a 327-token one and dashboard-create 316. Over the
friction session notes were 7,807 tokens of write echoes, repeated word
for word. The notes' own offers (alerts, subscriptions) already say to
make them once per conversation, so the first copy is the one the agent
acts on.

Generated handlers now call withAgentNoteOnce(context, toolName, ...),
which marks `shown:agentNote:<tool>` in the existing session-scoped
store (keyed by MCP session id or conversation id, set-if-absent, so
parallel calls show it once) and adds the note only the first time.
Later calls keep the same shape without it. A request with no session
(stateless, CLI) or a failing store gets the note every time, as before.

The insight-create note also told the agent to call insight-query with
the new short_id after saving. On the friction session that re-ran
queries the agent had tested moments earlier and returned identical
rows (4 calls, 566 tokens). The note now says to read the value from
the tested query and to call insight-query only for a query that was
saved untested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
